    "title": "Everything Coachella headliner Karol G sang during her historic set",
    "text": "It was a historic night for Colombian singer Karol G, who became the first Latina to headline the Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival.Latin pride was front and center on the Coachella Stage, Sunday, April 12, along with plenty of surprises throughout the night. The Colombian superstar shined a spotlight on women throughout her set and turned the festival grounds into a major dance party.Even her special guests brought girl power onto the stage. She first welcomed special guest Mariah Angeliq and turned the heat up with their sultry collab \"El Makinon.\" Later on, her pal Becky G joined the fun on \"MAMIII\" (which they also sang together during Karol G's Coachella debut in 2022).One of Karol G's more visually captivating set pieces involved a rock pit in the middle of the crowd filled with water, in which she and her female dancers splashed around in to \"Bandida entrenada.\" The women later channeled Amazonian goddesses as they rocked out to \"TQG\" (sans Shakira, sadly).Karol G 'stands for' immigrants in joyful, historic Coachella setAt the same time, Latino pride took center stage. She emerged in a feather headdress and top and skirt with the colors of the Colombian flag for her song \"Tropicoqueta.\" For a spotlight on Puerto Rico, Karol G invited rapper Wisin to come out and perform a medley of songs, including \"Pam Pam,\" \"Saoco,\" \"Mayor Que Yo\" and \"Rakata.\" Though Daddy Yankee was not on stage, his presence was also felt as many of his collaborations were featured.Based on Karol G's body language, she was feeling herself as she moved her hips to \"Un gatito me llamó\" – at one point she answered a phone call and said she was busy at Coachella – and \"OKI DOKI.\"Due to a late start, the singer had to cut her set short and head straight into her electrifying finale of \"Provenza,\" filled with all her dancers jumping around the runway, Karol G waving a Colombian flag and an explosion of fireworks filling the night sky.We'll have to wait until next week to see what the full set looks like, but her Sunday set was a beautiful and meaningful sendoff to a special weekend in the desert.Here's everything Karol G sang during her Weekend 1 performance:\"Latina Foreva\"\"Un Gatita Me Llamo\"\"Oki Doki\"\"Tá OK\"\"El Makinon\" (with special guest Mariah Angeliq)\"S91\"\"Que rico mambo\" (band only)\"Tropicoqueta\"\"Papasito\"\"Son de la Negra\" (performed by an all-female mariachi group)\"Ese Hombre Es Malo\"\"Mamiii\" (with special guest Becky G)\"A Su Boca La Amo (Interlude)\"\"Gatúbela\"\"Bandida Entrenada\"\"Ojos Ferrari\"\"Pam Pam\" (cover of Wisin & Yandel featuring special guest Wisin)\"Saoco\" (cover of Wisin & Yandel featuring special guest Wisin)\"Mayor Que Oh\" (cover of Baby Ranks, Daddy Yankee, Tonny Tún Tún, Wisin, Yandel & Héctor featuring special guest Wisin)\"Rakata\" (cover of Wisin & Yandel featuring special guest Wisin)\"Ivonny Bonita\"\"TQG\"\"Amargura\"\"Tusa\"\"Si Antes Te Hubiera Conocido\"\"Provenza\"Ema Sasic covers entertainment and health in the Coachella Valley. Reach her at ema.sasic@desertsun.com or on Twitter @ema_sasic. This article originally appeared on Palm Springs Desert Sun: Karol G full Coachella 2026 setlist – 'El Makinon' 'Mamiii,' more",
